{
  "_comment": [
    "Configuration for the Approvals slide, which is generated ENTIRELY from the ASTA Excel export.",
    "Approval Status.xlsx is no longer used. Future projects should only need changes HERE.",
    "",
    "BRANCH DETECTION — the approval branch is found by NAME, never by row number or depth (it sits at",
    "depth 1 in Harohalli, 2 in Blue in Green/TMFT and 3 in Violet Hill).",
    "  branch.primary / branch.aliases : names that identify the statutory-approval branch",
    "  branch.exclude                  : look-alike branches that must NOT be used — notably",
    "                                    'Approval Drawings / Details', which is a DESIGN deliverable",
    "                                    branch (drawings), not statutory approvals.",
    "  Only the activities IMMEDIATELY BELOW the branch become rows (one approval = one row).",
    "  childExclude drops non-approval children such as drawing/documentation/closure-milestone rows.",
    "",
    "STAGE COLUMNS — the four tick columns are matched against the approval's own activities by",
    "keyword; a tick is shown only when the matched activity is 100% complete.",
    "",
    "FINISH ACTIVITY — the Actual/Projected Finish comes from the approval's completion activity,",
    "chosen in the declared priority order (Issued → Approved → Sanction → Certificate → Clearance →",
    "the last activity in the branch). Baseline Finish comes from that same activity; if it has none,",
    "the cell is left blank. Nothing is ever fabricated — unresolved items are listed in",
    "approval_validation.md.",
    "",
    "overrides lets a specific approval name declare its own preferred finish activity, e.g. Layout."
  ],
