  "masterListComment": [
    "PER-PROJECT approval lists. There is NO global list: the previous PPT for a project is the source of truth for",
    "WHICH approvals appear, how many, their names and their order, and different projects legitimately differ.",
    "",
    "Precedence, highest first:",
    "  1. the uploaded previous/reference PPT for THIS project — read off its own Approvals Status slide;",
    "  2. masterListByProject, when a key matches this project's name — a pinned list for a project whose previous",
    "     deck is not being uploaded, transcribed from that project's own old PPT;",
    "  3. the project's own statutory approval branch in ITS OWN Excel schedule.",
    "",
    "Never a list borrowed from another project. Step 3 is per-project too — it reads that project's schedule — and",
    "the report says plainly when it was used, because a schedule-derived list can be renamed or merged by the",
    "planner and is not what the business tracks.",
    "",
    "'name' is what the slide prints and is never taken from the Excel. 'match' locates the task and never renames.",
    "A hint may be a string, an array (all terms), or {all, any, none}; terms of three characters or fewer match as",
    "whole words. Hints are tried in order, first hit wins.",
    "",
    "WHY \"TR Mills - Chamrajpet\" IS PINNED HERE.",
    "That project's previous deck stores its ENTIRE Approvals table as a flat PNG picture: slide 8 holds one",
    "24.68in x 9.92in image and no table, and the string \"AAI\" appears nowhere in any of the file's 98 parts.",
    "The 12 approval names it prints therefore cannot be read out of it by any amount of parsing. They are",
    "transcribed here from that slide exactly as it shows them, in its order.",
    "",
    "This entry fixes only WHICH rows appear, their WORDING and their ORDER. Every date, tick and status still",
    "comes from the Excel through the normal matching logic. The match hints below only LOCATE a task in the",
    "export - they never rename a row - and they are the same hints already proven on the other project that",
    "tracks the same 12 statutory approvals.",
    "",
    "It is a FALLBACK, not an override: an uploaded previous PPT whose Approvals slide has real text always wins.",
    "Once a GENERATED deck exists for this project its Approvals slide IS a real table, so from then on the list",
    "is read from the previous deck automatically and this entry stops being consulted."
  ],
